# Explainable AI for Fraud Detection

Detect → Explain → Act.

A credit card fraud detection system that flags suspicious transactions
and explains *why* using SHAP, so analysts can trust and act on each alert.

## Problem
Fraud is rare (492 of 284,807 transactions in the ULB dataset, 0.17%),
so accuracy is misleading. Black-box models also give analysts no reason
to trust a flag.

## Approach
Transaction data → Preprocessing → ML model → Fraud/Genuine prediction
→ SHAP explanation → Analyst decision

- Models: Logistic Regression, Random Forest, XGBoost
- Imbalance-aware evaluation: Precision, Recall, F1, PR-AUC
- Global SHAP: which features matter overall
- Local SHAP: why one specific transaction was flagged

## Live demo
`index.html` is an interactive prototype. Change a transaction and see
the fraud score, SHAP-style explanation, and analyst actions.
Note: the demo uses a simplified hand-weighted model for illustration.

## Business impact
Faster reviews, fewer false alarms, audit-ready decisions, more trust.

## Future scope
Real-time streaming, federated learning, counterfactual explanations,
drift monitoring.

## Dataset
[ULB Credit Card Fraud Detection](https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/mlg-ulb/creditcardfraud)

